From: abhay-byte <abhay02delhi@gmail.com>
Date: 2026-10-11
Subject: [PATCH jm-v9 029] panvk: v9 enable and override the primitive index when shaders use it biblioklept

Purpose: PanProbe vs_viewport_index E/F/G failed on the G57.
Root cause (002, exposed by 012/014/015): the v9 MALLOC_VERTEX primitive
descriptor never set primitive_index_enable/override. The FS read an
unenabled primitive index, and with the TES viewport passthrough writing
PRIMITIVE_ID the G57 dropped every primitive whose ID was not 0.
Fix: enable when the FS reads or the raster shader writes the ID, override
when the raster shader writes it (CSF rule, Noysz 0067). v9 only.
---

diff --git a/src/panfrost/vulkan/jm/panvk_vX_cmd_draw.c b/src/panfrost/vulkan/jm/panvk_vX_cmd_draw.c
index c5605c5..c9e910e 100644
--- a/src/panfrost/vulkan/jm/panvk_vX_cmd_draw.c
+++ b/src/panfrost/vulkan/jm/panvk_vX_cmd_draw.c
@@ -2370,6 +2370,16 @@ v9_emit_malloc_vertex_job(struct panvk_cmd_buffer *cmdbuf,
          cfg.index_type = MALI_INDEX_TYPE_NONE;
       cfg.primitive_restart = info->index.restart_enable;
       cfg.secondary_shader = secondary_shader;
+      /* gl_PrimitiveID (Noysz 0067, CSF): the HW primitive index for the
+       * FS, overridden by the value the raster VS writes (GS, TES or
+       * viewport passthrough). A written ID needs the override even when
+       * the FS does not read it: without it the G57 drops every primitive
+       * whose ID is not 0 (TES viewport-select draws of 2+ patches). */
+      const bool writes_prim_id =
+         (vs->info.outputs_written & VARYING_BIT_PRIMITIVE_ID) != 0;
+      cfg.primitive_index_enable =
+         writes_prim_id || (fs && fs->info.fs.reads_primitive_id);
+      cfg.primitive_index_override = writes_prim_id;
    }
    pan_section_pack(job.cpu, MALLOC_VERTEX_JOB, INSTANCE_COUNT, cfg) {
       cfg.count = info->instance.count;
